# ── Build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pio/
.pioenvs/
.piolibdeps/
*.o
*.elf

# ── Reference repos (large, vendored upstream) ─────────────────────────
# Cloned for reading patterns, not part of this project's history.
docs/references/

# ── Recorded data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runs are streamed over USB serial to the host, so raw captures normally
# never land in the repo. These rules cover the case where a CSV is copied
# in for review: raw dumps and generated figures are bulky, while the
# extracted feature set is small and worth keeping.
data/raw/
data/figures/
!data/features/
data/features/*.csv

# ── Captured baseline ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Measured mu/sigma are committed: they are the evidence behind every
# threshold in the report.
tools/baseline.json

# ── Editor / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*~